      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Niska, a tech company, has opened an ice cream shop in Australia. What’s unusual about this shop? Well, you won’t see any human shop assistants there. The shop, instead, is operated by three robots. Pepper, Eka, and Tony serve people their favourite icy snacks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The robots dance and wave flags to welcome customers. Pepper looks like a human. It was created by SoftBank, a tech company in Japan. The robot can "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "track",
            "ref": "v-track"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " eye contact, express emotions, and have simple conversations with people. At Niska’s ice cream shop, Pepper’s task is to talk to customers and take orders. Eka is a robot arm. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scoops",
            "ref": "v-scoop"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " ice cream. Tony, meanwhile, pours chocolate and nuts on top of the scoop."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Kate Orlova is Niska’s C.E.O. She says the company aims to improve people’s shopping experience. The ice cream shop is just the beginning. “We’d love to see robots in every store,” she adds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In a recent Australian survey, half of the workers said their jobs had changed because of "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "automation",
            "ref": "v-automation"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But Orlova says Niska’s robots were not created to take the place of human workers. Instead, they were designed to improve the customer experience. “Robots can’t completely replace human beings. However, robots are good at doing "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "repetitive",
            "ref": "v-repetitive"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tasks, such as scooping ice cream,” Orlova explains. “With the help of robots, human workers can be freed up to focus on creative tasks.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Would you want to order ice cream from robots? What do you think of Orlova’s plan? How do you think robots will change our daily lives? What can I do for you?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
